{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"dd057909e3ae43c6cf9b91469de8193cdbae4de233156a2500d604f49cf745f9","digest":{"component_or_area":"lock subsystem (src/rebar/_store/lock.py)","key_entities":["canonical_tracker","src/rebar/_store/lock.py:81-84","lock.py:289",".ticket-write.lock",".ticket-write.lock.d","acquire()","os.path.realpath","tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py"],"problem_keywords":["lock identity","symlink","realpath","canonicalization","cross-process locking","mutual exclusion","test coverage"],"propositions":["canonical_tracker (os.path.realpath) is the lock-path anchor that ensures symlinked-path and real-path callers contend on the same lock file, but this invariant has zero test coverage.","Two independent acquire() calls—one via real path, one via symlink—must mutually exclude in both directions, deterministically validated by bounded timeout and guaranteed lock contention.","Holding a lock acquired via the real path should cause a second acquire() via symlink to raise LockTimeout (with timeout=1, attempts=1), then succeed after release.","Holding a lock acquired via symlink should cause a second acquire() via real path to raise LockTimeout, then succeed after release, proving bidirectional lock identity."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821818485752698,"uuid":"4e31b515-d53e-428d-a74a-2ee4c1c44c33"}